<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">Peru-Bolivian Confederation</h1><p class="st-meta">1836 CE – 1839 CE · capital Tacna</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Andrés de Santa Cruz's union of Peru and Bolivia, which threatened the balance of power in South America and was destroyed by Chile in 1839.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1835 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru's</a> president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luis-jose-de-orbegoso">Luis José de Orbegoso</a> asked the Bolivian president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andres-de-santa-cruz">Andrés de Santa Cruz</a> for help against rebels. Santa Cruz invaded, defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agustin-gamarra">Agustín Gamarra</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/felipe-santiago-salaverry">Felipe Santiago Salaverry</a> in 1835 and 1836, and divided Peru into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/north-peruvian-republic">North Peruvian Republic</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/south-peruvian-republic">South Peruvian Republic</a>, which joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-bolivia">Republic of Bolivia</a> in a confederation.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-tacna">Pact of Tacna</a> of 1837 made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andres-de-santa-cruz">Santa Cruz</a> Supreme Protector, with broad powers over foreign affairs and the army. He introduced legal codes modelled on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon's</a> and promoted trade. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-chile">Chile</a>, under the influence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-portales">Diego Portales</a>, saw the confederation as a threat, and Chile declared war in December 1836, followed by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/argentine-confederation">Argentine Confederation</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-manuel-de-rosas">Rosas</a> in 1837. Peruvian exiles and many in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a> resented Bolivian dominance.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>A Chilean army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-bulnes">Manuel Bulnes</a>, joined by Peruvian exiles, defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andres-de-santa-cruz">Santa Cruz</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-yungay">Yungay</a> on 20 January 1839. The confederation was dissolved, and Santa Cruz went into exile. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-bolivia">Bolivia</a> were never united again, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-chile">Chile</a> emerged as the leading power on the Pacific coast.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/peru-bolivian-confederation.jpg" alt="Peru-Bolivian Confederation" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Huhsunqu · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Peru-Bolivian_Confederation.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1836 CE – 1839 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tacna</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Andrés de Santa Cruz</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish, Quechua, Aymara</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/peru">Peru</a>, <a href="/countries/bolivia">Bolivia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Peru–Bolivian Confederation, Confederación Perú-Boliviana</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1838&amp;focus=peru-bolivian-confederation" aria-label="Peru-Bolivian Confederation on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2775 2847 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Peru-Bolivian Confederation lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3095 3103L2883 2883M3095 3103L3235 3140M3095 3103L2883 2883M3095 3103L3095 3103"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2883 2883h0M3235 3140h0M2883 2883h0M3095 3103h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3095 3103h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3095 3103h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tacna. <a href="/atlas?year=1838&amp;focus=peru-bolivian-confederation">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
